[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Public API surface (`c_src/include/driver.h`), complete:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m void driver(int x);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is exactly **one** public entry point and it is simultaneously the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lowest-level one — there is no convenience wrapper layered over a lower API, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "exercise the low-level entry points, not just the wrappers" is satisfied by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m calling `driver` itself.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Runtime options / modes / flags: **none**. Grep found no global/static state, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m setters, no option struct, no `#ifdef`-gated behaviour, no environment reads.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only compile-time preprocessor directives are the `#include` and the header
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m include guard.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Body, complete:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m for (int i = 0, j = 0; i < x; i++, j += 2) {
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     printf("%d %d\n", i, j);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axes the code actually distinguishes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | why it is an axis | values that matter |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |------|-------------------|--------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | sign of `x` | `i < x` with `i` starting at 0 decides zero vs. non-zero iterations | negative, zero, positive |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | magnitude of `x` | number of `printf` calls; also determines the **decimal width** of `i` and `j` in `%d`, which is the only formatting variation the code can produce | 1, 2..9, 10..99, ... up to 7+ digits |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | digit-width skew between `i` and `j` | `j == 2*i`, so `j` gains a decimal digit before `i` does; crossing `j`'s power-of-ten boundaries is a distinct output shape | `x` near 5, 50, 500, 5000, ... |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `stdout` buffer boundary | `printf` to a fully-buffered stream flushes on 4096-byte boundaries; output must be identical regardless of where lines straddle the boundary | `x` chosen so total bytes straddle 4 KiB / 64 KiB |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | signed overflow of `j` | `j += 2` overflows `int` at `i == 2^30` (UB in C) | `x > 2^30` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | call sequencing / residual state | the function has no statics, so repeated and interleaved C/Rust calls must be independent | repeat, alternate C→Rust→C |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are no other axes: no input buffers, no element types, no widths, no byte
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m order, no counts, no formats. The cross-product below is the full set of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m combinations the C treats differently, pruned to those distinctions.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** drawn from a fixed-seed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m xorshift PRNG (seed `0x5EED_1234_ABCD_F00D`), not a single hand-picked value.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "C-vs-Rust byte-identical stdout" is the assertion in every row.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | #   | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C1  | `driver` | `x` = every value in `-8..=64` exhaustively (empty / one / few / many, plus the whole sign transition) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C2  | `driver` | `x` randomized in `1..=9` — single-digit `i`, `j` crosses from 1 to 2 digits at `i>=5` | [x] |
